        "NET0037",
        "GND"
      ],
      "observed": "The EPD driver schematic contains four SS2040FL diodes (U4, U5, U6, U8) in the voltage multiplier chain.",
      "expected": "The specification lists exactly three SS2040FL diodes (U1, U2, U3) for the EPD charge-pump circuit, matching the PDI reference design for the G1 group.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "EPD_Driver.kicad_sch: U4, U5, U6, U8 are all SS2040FL diodes connected in series for the charge pump."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "U1/U2/U3 SS2040FL Schottky diodes (SOD-123FL) ... PDI doc specifies 3× SS2040FL diodes for this exact circuit"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The additional diode stage increases the output voltage of the charge pump, potentially overvolting the e-paper display panel.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic contains a critical bridging error where the Ethernet jack (J9) is shorted to the MicroSD card interface (J4) via shared nets (NET0012, 0017, 0021, 0026), contradicting the spec's description of unconnected Ethernet pads. Additionally, the EPD charge pump uses four diodes instead of the specified three."
}

